              "question": "<p>Direct acting cholinergic drugs of the PNS act like acetylcholine on the muscarinic receptors. Indirect acting cholinergic drugs inhibit the enzyme acetylcholinesterase, that breaks down acetylcholine in the synaptic cleft, allowing the actual nerurotransmitter acetylcholine to remain in the synaptic cleft longer.</p>\n"
