              "a11yRetry": "Retry the task. Reset all responses and start the task over again.",
              "textField": "There are selective receptors in the sympathetic nervous system that are termed Alpha 1, Alpha 2, Beta 1 and Beta 2 receptors. Although the selective nature of the parasympathetic nervous system has not been elucidated as well, we do know a bit about the selective nature of the PNS. *M1* receptors are found in the brain, *M2* receptors are found in the heart, and *M3* receptors are responsible for bronchoconstriction, micturition and defecation, pupil constriction, and relaxation of the GIT. *M4 and M5* receptors are not fully elucidated."
